WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.725
What does the boundary look
like on the Marketplace?

2
00:00:02.725 --> 00:00:07.339
Read on November 1, 2026:
ServiceNow's Government Community

3
00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:11.200
Cloud is FedRAMP certified
at High, on the JAB path.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.870
ServiceNow's commercial cloud
has no listing of its own,

5
00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.625
and some agencies run on it.

6
00:00:16.625 --> 00:00:21.813
SailPoint Identity Security Cloud is
certified at Moderate, on the agency path.

7
00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:26.674
And IdentityIQ, the self-hosted
product, has no listing of its own.

8
00:00:26.674 --> 00:00:30.102
The interim path: on
ServiceNow's commercial cloud,

9
00:00:30.102 --> 00:00:35.896
the authorizing official decides whether
identity tasks may run there before a move,

10
00:00:35.896 --> 00:00:39.487
and, as design guidance,
payloads stay to identifiers.

11
00:00:39.487 --> 00:00:44.530
Where a feature's presence in SailPoint's
authorized environment is unconfirmed,

12
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:49.560
build Gates 3 to 6 in the sandbox and hold
production until SailPoint confirms it.
